/// | the same held open | `:thump` and a blank line every fifteen seconds, nothing else while nothing happens |
/// | the second person posts | `event: update`, `data:` the whole status as one line of JSON, as a timeline lists it |
/// | the second person changes it | `event: status.update`, the whole status as it now is, `edited_at` set |
/// | the second person reblogs a post of their own | `event: update`, **the reblog**, under its own id and `uri` (`…/activity`), the post inside it as `reblog` |
/// | the reblog taken back | `event: delete`, `data:` the reblog's own id, bare |
/// | the post deleted | `event: delete`, `data:` the post's id, bare. **A post that named the reader is said deleted twice** |
/// | the second person names the writer | to a sign-in holding `read:notifications` as well: `event: notification`, the whole notice; to one of `read:statuses` alone, nothing |
/// | `GET /api/v1/streaming/list?list=` a list of the writer's | 200, `:)` — the same line, for one list |
/// | `GET /api/v1/streaming/public/local` | 200, the same events for every public post of the server: here the same `update`, `status.update` and `delete` |
/// | the sign-in ended while a line is open | *doc — not asked*: the service ends the answer (`kill`), and the line closes as one dropped |
